@startuml
title Target — Capture upload, asynchronous inference, and Detection persistence
autonumber
actor "ESP32 camera" as Device
participant "Capture Ingestion API" as API
participant "Credential / request validation" as Auth
participant "Private object storage\n(S3 or MinIO)" as Storage
queue "RabbitMQ\ncaptures.raw" as RawQueue
participant "Python AI inference worker" as Worker
queue "RabbitMQ\ndetections.classified" as ResultQueue
participant "Detection consumer" as Consumer
database "PostgreSQL\nvia Prisma" as DB
queue "captures.dlq" as DLQ

Device -> API: POST /api/captures\nmetadata + image bytes
API -> Auth: authorize ingestion service\nand validate metadata
alt unauthorized or invalid metadata
  Auth --> API: reject
  API --> Device: 401/403 or 400
else accepted
  Auth --> API: CaptureMetadata
  API -> DB: verify deployment exists\n[planned domain validation]
  DB --> API: deployment and installedAt
  API -> Storage: store image privately
  Storage --> API: imageKey
  API -> RawQueue: publish persistent RawCaptureMessage
  API --> Device: 202 Accepted\neventId

  RawQueue -> Worker: deliver with bounded prefetch
  Worker -> Storage: fetch image by imageKey
  Storage --> Worker: image bytes
  alt image missing/corrupt or inference repeatedly fails
    Worker -> RawQueue: reject/retry according to policy
    RawQueue -> DLQ: route after configured retry limit
  else inference succeeds
    Worker -> Worker: run model inference
    Worker -> ResultQueue: publish ClassifiedResultMessage
    Worker --> RawQueue: acknowledge raw capture
    ResultQueue -> Consumer: deliver classification result
    Consumer -> Consumer: validate status and fields
    Consumer -> Storage: confirm image exists [planned]
    Consumer -> DB: persist immutable Detection
    DB --> Consumer: stored row or existing matching eventId
    Consumer --> ResultQueue: acknowledge message
  end
end

note over API,DLQ
  This flow is documented target behavior, not current implementation.
  Queue retry count/backoff and storage provider remain deployment decisions.
  The docs suggest a bounded retry policy and dead-letter routing.
end note
@enduml
